                "text": "The `ledger` CLI tool has been implemented in `src/ledger.py`. It correctly handles input parsing, command execution, and money formatting as specified.\n\n### Implementation Details:\n- **Input Parsing**: Reads from `stdin`, handles malformed lines by printing an error to `stderr` and exiting with code `2`.\n- **Money Formatting**: Uses the `decimal` module with `ROUND_HALF_UP` to ensure consistent two-decimal formatting.\n- **Commands**:\n    - `total`: Sums all amounts.\n    - `count`: Counts the number of records.\n    - `average`: Calculates the mean, handling the empty case.\n    - `categories`: Lists categories sorted by amount (descending) and name (ascending).\n    - `top N`: Lists the top `N` categories.\n    - `category NAME`: Displays the total for a specific category, exiting with code `1` if not found.\n- **Error Handling**: Invalid commands or missing arguments result in a usage error (exit code `2`).\n\n### Verification:\nThe implementation was verified with a test script covering:\n- `total` calculation.\n- `categories` sorting logic.\n- `category` lookup and error handling.\n- Malformed line detection.\n- Edge cases like empty input and `top N` where `N` exceeds the number of categories.\n\nAll tests passed successfully.",
